TASK W2-02 — the dpf state follower and ledger tail (C7, C13)
Repo /home/dev/work/dippe/dp-forge · base cac247d1 · package tools/dpf (run every command from the repo root)
You write the failing tests AND the implementation. Touch only the files under FILES.

WHY
`tools/dpf` shows one progress line per step and detects a pause, but it reads the pipeline's
files (state.json and ledger.jsonl) and starts its commands — nothing else. It needs a dpf-local
`RunState` (not the pipeline's zod schema) to read the cursor and step statuses, and a ledger
tail that reads by BYTE offset (C13: the start offset is the ledger's byte size) so it never
re-reads old rows. Ledger rows carry non-ASCII text (the residue texts use `—`), so a string
offset is NOT a byte offset: the tail works on a Buffer and decodes only complete lines.
This row builds both. It is read-only on the pipeline's files: it never writes them.

FILES
tools/dpf/src/run/state.ts          new
tools/dpf/src/follow/ledger.ts      new
tools/dpf/tests/run/state.test.ts   new
tools/dpf/tests/follow/ledger.test.ts new

